1
00:00:00,204 --> 00:00:02,300
You've done push-ups for months.

2
00:00:02,484 --> 00:00:03,892
Same twenty reps.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,107
Same chest.

4
00:00:05,323 --> 00:00:06,333
Same arms.

5
00:00:06,613 --> 00:00:07,215
Hey.

6
00:00:07,065 --> 00:00:08,311
That's personal.

7
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:09,946
It's not your genetics.

8
00:00:10,204 --> 00:00:11,408
It's your push-up.

9
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:14,430
Most people make the same six mistakes,

10
00:00:14,495 --> 00:00:16,988
and each one quietly steals your strength.

11
00:00:17,269 --> 00:00:19,537
Fix them, and the same push-up starts

12
00:00:19,387 --> 00:00:21,171
building real muscle again.

13
00:00:21,452 --> 00:00:22,654
Six?

14
00:00:22,505 --> 00:00:24,020
I was hoping for one.

15
00:00:24,301 --> 00:00:26,622
Stay till the end, because mistake six

16
00:00:26,473 --> 00:00:29,730
is the one almost everyone makes, and

17
00:00:29,581 --> 00:00:31,439
it's the reason most people never get

18
00:00:31,290 --> 00:00:32,118
past twenty.

19
00:00:32,935 --> 00:00:33,806
Mistake one.

20
00:00:34,817 --> 00:00:36,891
Elbows flared out like a T.

21
00:00:37,172 --> 00:00:39,150
It feels easier, because your chest gets

22
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,138
a shorter range.

23
00:00:40,398 --> 00:00:42,751
But your shoulders take the load, and

24
00:00:42,602 --> 00:00:44,666
that's where push-up pain starts.

25
00:00:44,946 --> 00:00:47,408
So that clicking in my shoulder is...

26
00:00:47,258 --> 00:00:49,204
a feature?

27
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:50,440
It's a warning.

28
00:00:50,699 --> 00:00:53,311
Tuck your elbows to about forty-five degrees.

29
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:55,473
Think arrow, not T.

30
00:00:55,753 --> 00:00:57,903
Seen from above, your arms and your

31
00:00:57,753 --> 00:00:59,021
head make an arrow.

32
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:01,257
Your elbows brush past your ribs on

33
00:01:01,108 --> 00:01:02,708
the way down, not out to the

34
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:03,193
side.

35
00:01:03,473 --> 00:01:04,032
Arrow.

36
00:01:03,882 --> 00:01:04,634
Got it.

37
00:01:04,891 --> 00:01:06,161
I'm a weapon now.

38
00:01:06,978 --> 00:01:07,849
Mistake two.

39
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:10,215
Sagging hips.

40
00:01:10,495 --> 00:01:12,311
When your hips drop, your lower back

41
00:01:12,161 --> 00:01:14,150
takes the bend and your core switches

42
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:14,505
off.

43
00:01:14,763 --> 00:01:16,999
You're doing half a push-up and half

44
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:17,763
a back bend.

45
00:01:18,043 --> 00:01:19,838
Banana push-ups.

46
00:01:20,118 --> 00:01:20,881
Exactly.

47
00:01:21,011 --> 00:01:23,365
Squeeze your glutes and brace your stomach

48
00:01:23,215 --> 00:01:24,559
like someone's about to poke it.

49
00:01:24,817 --> 00:01:27,139
Head to heels, one straight line.

50
00:01:27,419 --> 00:01:28,473
Here's a quick check.

51
00:01:28,634 --> 00:01:30,344
Put a broomstick along your back.

52
00:01:30,602 --> 00:01:32,365
It should touch your head, your upper

53
00:01:32,215 --> 00:01:34,042
back and your hips at the same

54
00:01:33,892 --> 00:01:34,397
time.

55
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:36,548
I don't own a broomstick.

56
00:01:36,828 --> 00:01:38,559
Then film yourself from the side.

57
00:01:38,817 --> 00:01:40,021
The camera doesn't lie.

58
00:01:40,839 --> 00:01:41,860
Mistake three.

59
00:01:42,871 --> 00:01:43,870
Half reps.

60
00:01:44,151 --> 00:01:46,408
Most people stop halfway down, because the

61
00:01:46,258 --> 00:01:47,731
bottom is the hardest part.

62
00:01:47,989 --> 00:01:49,774
But the bottom is exactly where the

63
00:01:49,624 --> 00:01:52,182
chest is stretched, and stretched muscle under

64
00:01:52,032 --> 00:01:53,419
load is what grows.

65
00:01:53,699 --> 00:01:55,473
So the hard part is the good

66
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:55,827
part.

67
00:01:56,086 --> 00:01:56,741
Rude.

68
00:01:57,022 --> 00:01:58,913
Chest to a fist's height from the

69
00:01:58,763 --> 00:01:59,387
floor.

70
00:01:59,484 --> 00:02:00,365
Every rep.

71
00:02:00,624 --> 00:02:03,118
Ten full reps beat thirty half ones.

72
00:02:03,398 --> 00:02:04,838
And don't bounce off the bottom.

73
00:02:05,097 --> 00:02:06,763
Pause for one second down there.

74
00:02:07,022 --> 00:02:09,182
It feels brutal, and that's exactly why

75
00:02:09,032 --> 00:02:09,774
it works.

76
00:02:11,398 --> 00:02:12,430
Mistake four.

77
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:16,225
Hands too far forward, or too wide.

78
00:02:16,505 --> 00:02:18,430
Hands up by your face put your

79
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,677
wrists and shoulders in a bad spot.

80
00:02:20,935 --> 00:02:23,279
Too wide, and the range gets tiny.

81
00:02:23,559 --> 00:02:26,537
Hands just outside your shoulders, under your

82
00:02:26,387 --> 00:02:27,064
chest.

83
00:02:27,323 --> 00:02:30,150
Fingers spread wide, gripping the floor.

84
00:02:30,430 --> 00:02:32,548
If your wrists still hurt, turn your

85
00:02:32,398 --> 00:02:34,709
hands out a little, or do them

86
00:02:34,559 --> 00:02:35,569
on your fists.

87
00:02:35,828 --> 00:02:37,645
Wrist straight, pain gone.

88
00:02:37,925 --> 00:02:39,569
Fist push-ups again?

89
00:02:39,828 --> 00:02:41,204
Very action movie.

90
00:02:42,022 --> 00:02:42,956
Mistake five.

91
00:02:43,968 --> 00:02:44,881
The head drop.

92
00:02:45,161 --> 00:02:46,537
I call that the chicken.

93
00:02:46,817 --> 00:02:49,042
Your nose touches the floor, so it

94
00:02:48,892 --> 00:02:50,483
feels like a full rep.

95
00:02:50,742 --> 00:02:52,118
Your chest never got there.

96
00:02:52,398 --> 00:02:54,268
Look at the floor a little ahead

97
00:02:54,118 --> 00:02:55,999
of your hands, and keep your head

98
00:02:55,849 --> 00:02:56,946
in line with your body.

99
00:02:57,226 --> 00:02:59,107
Pretend you're holding an egg between your

100
00:02:58,957 --> 00:03:00,376
chin and your chest.

101
00:03:00,634 --> 00:03:02,258
Don't crush it, don't drop it.

102
00:03:03,075 --> 00:03:03,956
And the big one.

103
00:03:04,215 --> 00:03:05,247
Mistake six.

104
00:03:06,258 --> 00:03:09,064
Doing the same twenty push-ups forever.

105
00:03:09,344 --> 00:03:11,333
Your body adapts to what you ask.

106
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:13,935
If the ask never changes, the body

107
00:03:13,785 --> 00:03:14,688
never changes.

108
00:03:14,968 --> 00:03:16,978
So my push-ups got bored of me.

109
00:03:17,258 --> 00:03:19,032
Add one rep a week.

110
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:22,128
Or slow down: three seconds down.

111
00:03:22,387 --> 00:03:23,365
Or raise your feet.

112
00:03:23,624 --> 00:03:25,860
Small upgrades, every week.

113
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,053
Here's the ladder.

114
00:03:27,312 --> 00:03:28,430
Wall push-ups.

115
00:03:28,688 --> 00:03:29,827
Knee push-ups.

116
00:03:30,086 --> 00:03:31,311
Normal push-ups.

117
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:32,913
Slow push-ups.

118
00:03:33,172 --> 00:03:34,161
Feet up on a chair.

119
00:03:34,419 --> 00:03:36,731
Each step is harder, and each step

120
00:03:36,581 --> 00:03:37,569
builds more.

121
00:03:37,849 --> 00:03:39,892
So when twenty gets easy, I climb.

122
00:03:40,172 --> 00:03:40,967
Exactly.

123
00:03:41,226 --> 00:03:43,150
Easy means it's time to climb.

124
00:03:43,968 --> 00:03:46,075
So here's the perfect push-up, start to

125
00:03:45,925 --> 00:03:46,569
finish.

126
00:03:46,849 --> 00:03:48,064
Hands under your shoulders.

127
00:03:48,323 --> 00:03:49,645
Elbows at forty-five.

128
00:03:49,903 --> 00:03:51,655
Body in one straight line.

129
00:03:51,914 --> 00:03:52,752
Head neutral.

130
00:03:53,032 --> 00:03:55,344
Lower slowly until your chest is a

131
00:03:55,194 --> 00:03:56,483
fist from the floor.

132
00:03:56,742 --> 00:03:58,290
Then push the floor away.

133
00:03:58,570 --> 00:03:59,623
And breathe?

134
00:03:59,903 --> 00:04:01,591
Breathe in on the way down, out

135
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:02,193
on the way up.

136
00:04:03,011 --> 00:04:03,741
Here's a test.

137
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,430
Do one set of perfect push-ups right

138
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:06,763
now.

139
00:04:07,022 --> 00:04:08,655
Most people lose a third of their

140
00:04:08,505 --> 00:04:09,085
reps.

141
00:04:09,366 --> 00:04:11,204
So my thirty is really twenty?

142
00:04:11,484 --> 00:04:12,139
Probably.

143
00:04:12,398 --> 00:04:14,451
But that twenty builds real strength.

144
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,397
Comment your perfect-rep number.

145
00:04:16,677 --> 00:04:18,462
And no banana push-ups.

146
00:04:18,312 --> 00:04:19,289
We will know.
